Bend2 compiler port

This implementation targets Bend2 from bendlang/bend at revision
6018e28ecc67cf1fffc0c20c64b11023474c2df8 (2026-09-20).
https://github.com/bendlang/bend

The compiler algorithms in src/core, src/check, src/front, src/load and
src/back are implemented in Bend2. Their design follows the pinned upstream
language implementation and compiler. Upstream TypeScript is a bootstrap and
validation dependency; ordinary compiler execution does not invoke it.

The native execution runtime and effect implementations under
src/runtime/native are extracted from upstream bend2/comp.ts and bend2/effs.
They are retained in C/Metal/CUDA/JavaScript as execution runtimes, with their
Apache-2.0 license and origin record. dist/base.bend is the pinned upstream
standard library. The JavaScript runtime also follows upstream primitive and
foreign-effect conventions. These dependencies are not claimed as new work.

Upstream test programs and expected outputs referenced by conformance reports
belong to their respective contributors. See UPSTREAM-LICENSE for the upstream
Apache-2.0 license, and src/runtime/native/ORIGIN.md for runtime provenance.
The new implementation and tooling are provided under Apache-2.0 (LICENSE).

The earlier surface-only prototype remains in src/compiler.bend and
its executable dist/bend2c.mjs for regression and bootstrap comparisons.
The typed compiler is a separate implementation. Compatibility claims must be
read with the recorded test results; source availability alone is not evidence
of full upstream equivalence.
